[Music]  hey everyone welcome to another  installment of harry potter theory today  we're going to once again be discussing  the third installment of the fantastic  beasts franchise fantastic beasts  secrets of dumbledore the film just came  out in north america a few days ago and  by this point it's come out in theaters  across most of the world so i thought  it'd be a good time to release a list of  my pros and cons limiting myself to just  five of each if you want a full scale  review and breakdown i've done that as  well i'll leave a link down in the  pinned comment i'll be alternating pros  with cons as to not overly hype up or  bog down the experience let's get into  it  pro number one actors characters and  casting  starting things off on a good note the  first thing that i'd like to point out  is that both the acting and casting in  the fantastic beast films is excellent  before this latest film jude lore  already smashed it as young dumbledore  as did eddie redmayne who plays newt's  commander however this latest film  includes several new main actors to the  fantastic beasts series including maz  mickelson and jessica williams maz  mickelson took over for johnny depp in  the role of grindelwald and man all i  can say is that he absolutely killed it  i thought johnny was good too but i'm  personally of the impression that maz  was made for this role his seamless  performance as grindelwald was a huge  pro for me and it honestly felt as if he  had actually been in the previous films  on a separate note i felt that the  inclusion of new witch ulalli hicks was  a great choice  hicks played by jessica williams is an  ilvermorny professor who ends up helping  the protagonists and there is a certain  charm surrounding her character i think  she was a wonderful addition  con number one no tina or barely any  tina anyway when the secrets of  dumbledore trailers were first coming  out and no one could find tina goldstein  in them it was a bit worrisome however  as time went on and as i thought about  it more i figured she had to be in the  film i said this to myself because a  queenie her sister is in the trailer  b she was a large part of the first two  films and c we know that she eventually  marries newt  so bearing all that in mind i must say  that i was quite surprised when tina was  so very absent from the story the  explanation tina was promoted this  doesn't make sense at all her sister is  in danger the wizarding world is in  danger and newt her love interest is in  danger why on earth wouldn't she be  there to help what could be more  important she shows up at the end but  i'd rather she didn't with that  explanation regardless of how you feel  about tina's character this was a big  con  pro number two soundtrack i'm going to  keep this one brief as it speaks for  itself the music  james newton howard did the soundtrack  for the secrets of dumbledore and he  absolutely smashed it capturing the  magic perfectly  a poor soundtrack can so profoundly  impact the feel of the film  with the film like harry potter which  depicts a magical world this becomes  even more important  no complaints at all from me here con  number two chillin bows to dumbledore  in this film we're introduced to a  creature called a chillin which holds  the special ability to recognize those  that are pure of heart  in order to acknowledge that an  individual is pure of heart the chilean  will bow to them and this is an  important part of the election that  takes place in the film at one point  when the real chilean surfaces it walks  around the election site trying to find  a worthy witch or wizard and finally it  stops at dumbledore who would then bows  to  this doesn't make sense to me because  it's highlighted in the film that barely  anyone is entirely pure of heart and  that for the chilling to bow to you  you've got to basically be a saint this  completely contradicts dumbledore's  character who we know to have quite a  dark history  dumbledore is mostly good these days but  he certainly knows saint particularly if  he at any time plotted to take over the  wizarding world i don't quite understand  this  pro 3 brings magic back to the franchise  i mention this in my full review but i  want to emphasize that this film felt  way more harry pottery  yes the fantastic beast films are  prequels and separate important  distinctions to be aware of but that  doesn't mean that filmmakers can't  bridge the gap between the two film  franchises  though still very different feeling than  harry potter itself i definitely felt  magic in this film that the previous two  installments were lacking  this was a huge one for me  con number three nagini some people  probably didn't even notice this but  nagini was completely stripped from this  film and there was absolutely no  explanation  in the previous film nagini became quite  close with credence and it also started  to look like she would become a more  prominent character  we know that later on once the harry  potter stories timeline sets in that  nagini becomes a prevalent character  voldemort's trusty serpentine companion  but when the crimes of grindelwald ended  nagini wasn't yet trapped as a snake the  result of her maledictus curse  so it's confusing that she's just been  removed with no in-universe explanation  pro number four expanding the dumbledore  family i mentioned this in my review as  well but i think it's extremely exciting  that one of the most enigmatic wizarding  families the dumbledores are having an  adjustment made to their family tree  time will tell what happens to credence  but this does open up a big can of worms  and it's quite exciting con number four  queenie's redemption  in the last film queenie goldstein  tina's sister has a large argument with  her now husband jacob over his  unwillingness to marry her this leads to  her disoperating to paris where she ends  up having a run-in with grindelwald's  acolytes  long story short queenie makes an  extremely misguided decision when she  chooses to join grindelwald in the hopes  of building a future where she can be  with jacob  queenie seemed good up to this point and  she can read minds so this decision of  hers didn't make much sense this brings  us to the secrets of dumbledore  queenie's role as one of grindelwald's  acolytes is essentially to read the mind  of credence who grindelwald hopes he  will be able to use as a weapon against  dumbledore  beyond that queenie's significance in  the film is low but what i found  annoying is just how quickly queenie was  redeemed it seems like one moment she  was evil and the next she was back with  jacob as if nothing had happened i don't  think that she necessarily deserved to  be redeemed quite so quickly and i wish  they focused on this more pro number  five the right direction  though the secrets of dumbledore film is  being criticized quite heavily i do feel  as though these films are really  beginning to head in the right direction  where the first film contributed very  little to the harry potter universe as a  whole we're progressively getting more  and more of a sense of what life in the  wizarding world was like before harry  potter and more importantly what the  foundations of things were like  we're getting deep into the law and i'm  here for it con number five use of karma  in this film dumbledore gives all of the  protagonists a different task the  ultimate goal of defeating confusing  grindelwald one of these protagonists is  yusuf karma whose task is basically to  infiltrate grindelwald's people yusuf's  role in the film seems very  insignificant and unimportant only  really helping out at one moment towards  the end when he helps lally and theseus  in defeating grindelwald's acolytes  honestly i think it was just a waste of  his character  and that's it for this video  do you agree with these what are your  pros and cons comment down below until  next time remember we must all face the  choice between what is right and what is  easy  you

